(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// bytearray (Objects/bytearrayobject.c), added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b; PY5b's report:"] [11 1 "// \"bytearray and memoryview ... not done\"): a mutable bytes. _collections_abc, and so collections.abc,"] [12 1 "// typing, os, copy and every module importing them, need the type at import. Its own slots and mutating"] [13 1 "// methods are here; bytes' other methods are bytes.go's, called on a copy, their bytes results made"] [14 1 "// bytearrays (bytearray's methods return bytearrays where bytes' return bytes)."] [21 1 "// ByteArray is a bytearray; exports is its ob_exports (queue 249, buffer_export.go): the memoryviews holding it."] [27 1 "// bytearrayExports (PYI_BYTEARRAY_EXPORTS=1) counts a bytearray's exports. Off by default (queue 249): _pyio, pyi's io,"] [28 1 "// passes temporary views of bytearrays and then resizes them (FileIO.readall's memoryview(result)[n:] then"] [29 1 "// result.resize), so every file read would ask Go's collector whether those views died, and under goi a view its"] [30 1 "// registers still hold made the resize fail (BufferError in an import's get_data). CPython's C io takes no Python views."] [33 1 "// Exports makes a bytearray a counting exporter (buffer_export.go) when bytearrayExports; nil (no count) otherwise."] [41 1 "// canResize is _canresize: BufferError while a view holds the buffer."] [46 1 "// resizeTo is a size change to n (PyByteArray_Resize's check: none when the size stays)."] [56 1 "// BytesLike makes a bytearray a bytes-like object for asBytes (bytes.go)."] [59 1 "// NewByteArray is a bytearray holding b (not copied)."] [63 13 "// the bytearray or subclass instance iterated (bytearrayiter_reduce)"] [80 1 "// toByteArrays makes bytes' results bytearrays: a bytes, the bytes in a list or tuple."] [99 1 "// byteValue is _getbytevalue (Objects/bytearrayobject.c): the byte o is as an int (__index__'s own errors propagate),"] [100 1 "// ValueError beyond range(0, 256) (an int too large for a long too)."] [113 1 "// maxBytesAlloc is what pyi allocates for one bytes or bytearray (larger: MemoryError, where Go's make panics)."] [116 1 "// sizeBytes is a size n for a new buffer: MemoryError past maxBytesAlloc (PyErr_NoMemory)."] [124 1 "// fromObject fills an emptied bytearray from o as bytearray's __init__ does after the int and str cases: the"] [125 1 "// buffer (__buffer__'s too), else an iterable of ints appended one by one (so a generator sees the bytes made so"] [126 1 "// far), each by _getbytevalue; a failure empties it again."] [141 2 "// an exact list or tuple is sized first and a failure resets it to empty (the uninitialized bytes are not"] [142 2 "// exposed); the slow path keeps what it appended before the failure"] [163 1 "// bufferData is a copy of the bytes o exports through the buffer protocol (a bytes-like object, or a class's"] [164 1 "// __buffer__, released once read); found is false for an object that exports none."] [181 1 "// pyNumberCheck is PyNumber_Check: an int, a float, a complex, or a class with __index__, __int__ or __float__."] [188 1 "// sliceValues is what a slice assignment takes from values that are not a bytearray (bytearray_ass_subscript): a"] [189 1 "// number or a str is a TypeError, anything else is converted as bytearray(values) does."] [201 1 "// allocSize is bytearray.__alloc__: the bytes allocated, one more than the size (the trailing NUL) once anything is"] [202 1 "// held, 0 for an empty buffer that never held any."] [212 39 "// bytearray_repr: a subclass's name"] [224 41 "// bytearray___init__'s PyByteArray_Resize(self, 0)"] [227 13 "// emptied first of all: a failure below leaves it empty (gh-91153's reinit)"] [228 3 "// encoding and errors as clinic's const char *: str only"] [356 5 "// bytearray_setslice_linear: a growth either way is a resize"] [362 5 "// in place when the length is kept or the slice is the tail (queue 210: _pyio's BytesIO writes"] [363 5 "// b[pos:pos+n] at its end, and a copy of the whole buffer for each write made StringIO quadratic)"] [368 6 "// a shrink stays in the buffer (bytearray_setslice_linear's memmove: the allocation is kept)"] [380 5 "// the extended slice deleted (needed == 0, a value of no bytes too): _canresize first, even for no item"] [405 3 "// bytearray_ass_subscript: the index, then the value (before the size check: its __index__ may"] [406 3 "// resize the bytearray, gh-91153), then the bounds"] [452 2 "// bytearray_irepeat (queue 249: in place, a resize; pyi made a new bytearray, so b *= n rebound b)"] [500 58 "// bytearray_mod through __rmod__"] [530 3 "// bytearray_extend_impl: a buffer goes straight to bytearray_setslice(self, size, size, ...), the size read"] [531 3 "// before the buffer is acquired (its __buffer__ may resize self: gh-153578, the data lands at the old end, clamped)"] [673 2 "// bytearray.take_bytes(n=None, /) (3.15, Objects/bytearrayobject.c's bytearray_take_bytes_impl; queue 237): the first n"] [674 2 "// bytes (negative: from the end, None: all) as bytes, the rest left in the bytearray"] [693 21 "// __index__ may have resized it"] [723 2 "// bytes' other methods, on a copy, their results made bytearrays (once bytes.go's are in its dict)"] [751 1 "// byteIndex is a bytearray's index k (negative from the end), CPython's errors."] [766 1 "// byteIndexRaw is a bytearray subscript that is not a slice, as PyNumber_AsSsize_t(index, PyExc_IndexError): an index"] [767 1 "// past a Py_ssize_t is an IndexError."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[71 28] [74 42] [128 35] [166 24] [191 22] [195 29] [224 26] [252 28] [280 32] [322 26] [328 24] [328 31] [341 26] [348 34] [358 29] [381 28] [386 25] [386 32] [400 24] [400 31] [413 28] [424 27] [446 42] [472 34] [480 13] [480 24] [512 42] [523 26] [555 32] [568 27] [598 26] [613 30] [623 26] [639 26] [646 26] [660 25] [663 26] [681 29] [705 27] [718 28] [718 35] [736 25] [769 22]]} (go/file "bytearray.go" :imports [


